  "description": "Aggregate the work that delivers this outcome: CLI and in-process tests use one definition of each fixture and reach process state only through the shared guards.\n\n## Background\n\nThis story groups the test-topology tasks that share one design surface, so they can be reviewed together once each has landed.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: One shared fixture spawns `jit` for every CLI test, and no test file defines its own binary locator, repository setup or id scraping from human-readable output.\n- [hard] REQ-02: Issue construction, the taxonomy repository and the memory executor each have one definition in shared test support, and the memory executor is set up by product initialisation.\n- [hard] REQ-03: Tests that need the shipped item kinds derive them from the shipped default package.\n- [hard] REQ-04: Tests reach the working directory and environment only through the shared scoped guards, and every test passes alone, in any order and in parallel.\n",
